TITLE:: ParaEQSpectrum
summary:: what an eq is working on, drawn behind its curve
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/ParaEQ, Classes/ParaEQView, Classes/ParaEQPanel, Classes/FFT

DESCRIPTION::
One FFT on the bus just after the eq, read back into the language a frame at a
time, and reduced to the loudest bin in each of 64 log spaced bands - a peak
reading of everything going through, honest about where the energy is, which is
what an eq is aimed by.

code::
spectrum = ParaEQSpectrum(eq);
spectrum.action = { { eqView.refresh }.defer };
spectrum.running = true;         // while the eq page is up
spectrum.levels;                 // 64 dB values, loud-fast and slow-falling
spectrum.freqs;                  // the frequency each one sits at
spectrum.free;                   // in window.onClose
::

Where it reads is the eq's business - link::Classes/FxUnit#-analysisPlacement::.
An eq with a node of its own is read just after that node; an eq driving an Ndef
at the tail of the Ndef's group, on the Ndef's bus; an eq driving a plain Synth
has no bus to read until its code::analysisBus:: is set. An eq that is off has
no picture, and nothing is analysed unless a window has asked - no synth, no
buffer, no polling.

The whole frame is read rather than reduced on the server: a band near the top
of the range covers a hundred bins, and a tone in it is in one of them, so
sampling a few would miss it.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: eq
A link::Classes/ParaEQ::, or nil for one to be pointed later.

METHOD:: on
A class wide switch - the panel's strong::spectrum:: box. Off, nothing is drawn
or analysed anywhere.

METHOD:: fftSize
4096.
METHOD:: numBands
64, log spaced between link::#*minFreq:: and link::#*maxFreq::.
METHOD:: pollRate
Frames a second read from the server. 15.
METHOD:: syncRate
How often the node is checked. 2.
METHOD:: floorDb
METHOD:: topDb
The scale the trace is drawn on: -78 and 6.
METHOD:: fallDb
METHOD:: peakFallDb
How fast the trace and the mark over it fall back, dB a second.
METHOD:: dbTrim
METHOD:: minFreq
METHOD:: maxFreq

METHOD:: rebuild
Forget everything worked out from the settings above, defs included, so a change
takes.

METHOD:: freqs
METHOD:: bandBins
METHOD:: fetchCount
METHOD:: defName
METHOD:: synthDef
METHOD:: normalise

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: eq
The eq analysed. Setting another moves the analyser and starts the trace again.

METHOD:: running
Whether a picture is being made at all.

METHOD:: visible
Running, switched on, and with somewhere to read.

METHOD:: levels
METHOD:: peaks
METHOD:: freqs
What the view draws.

METHOD:: levelAt
The level now at a frequency, in dB - the band it falls in - or nil before the
first frame: what the eq window's pointer readout says.
ARGUMENT:: freq

METHOD:: action
Called with the spectrum whenever a frame has been taken.

METHOD:: server

METHOD:: free
Stops, and gives the buffer back.
